<title>GERMANY: Buba's Welteke sees some leeway with EMU criteria.</title>
<headline>Buba's Welteke sees some leeway with EMU criteria.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Monday there was some leeway in interpreting two fiscal criteria nations need to meet to join economic and monetary union (EMU) to qualify for a single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;There is discretionary leeway in interpreting the two fiscal criteria for EMU and they are greater than often reported,&quot; Welteke told an audience.</p>
</text>
